# Solution Methods

### Method 1: Decoding with OpenSSL (Standard Method)
A Certificate Signing Request (CSR) is an ASN.1 structured file. To parse and read its details, you can use `openssl`:

```bash
openssl req -in readmycert.csr -noout -text
```

The output will display the metadata, and the flag is located under the **Subject's Common Name (CN)**:
```text
Subject: CN=picoCTF{read_mycert_373b4ab0}, name=ctfPlayer
```

