### Method 2: Manual Base64 Decoding (Without OpenSSL)
Since the metadata in the CSR structure (like the CN) is stored as plain ASCII text, you can decode the Base64 PEM payload directly to read the flag.

#### Bash/Linux Command:
```bash
grep -v "CERTIFICATE" readmycert.csr | tr -d '\n' | base64 -d | strings
```

#### Output:
```text
picoCTF{read_mycert_373b4ab0}
ctfPlayer
```

